  "name": "Jing ping (Dominica accordion band music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Village dance-band music of Dominica played on accordion, a tambal (frame drum), a gwaj (metal scraper) and the boumboum, a length of bamboo blown as a bass. Jing ping bands play the island's European-derived Creole dances, among them the quadrille, mazouk, polka, waltz and heel-and-toe, and the style later fed into bouyon; the vaksin card (a blown bamboo trumpet) stands in for the boumboum, the hand-drum card for the tambal and the scraper card for the gwaj.",
  "recipe": "classic modern jing ping, groove Percussion, Caribbean branch, tropical song functional song. accordion, hand drum source guayo source unspecified, vaksin. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
